# Night-shift triage configuration.
# Copy to ~/.config/topaz/nightshift.conf and adjust.
#
# TRIAGE_CMD is any command that reads the event digest on stdin and writes a
# markdown report on stdout. Point it at whatever analysis tool you prefer —
# an AI coding agent, a local model, or a plain script. If unset, raw digests
# are saved instead.
#
# The suggested triage instructions live in
# /usr/share/topaz-os/nightshift-prompt.md; most LLM CLIs accept them as a
# prompt argument, for example:
#
#   TRIAGE_CMD='some-agent --prompt "$(cat /usr/share/topaz-os/nightshift-prompt.md)"'
#
# TRIAGE_TIMEOUT is the maximum runtime in seconds (default 600).

#TRIAGE_CMD=''
#TRIAGE_TIMEOUT=600
